---
short_label: XIII.6
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a rational straight line is cut in extreme and mean ratio, then each of the segments is the irrational straight line called apotome.
----
proof:

Let *AB* be a rational straight line cut in extreme and mean ratio at *C,* and let *AC* be the greater segment.

I say that each of the straight lines *AC* and *CB* is the irrational straight line called apotome.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="70" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.6 diagram" src="propXIII6.gif"/></noscript>
